// An import naming a source file that is not there.
//
// It gets its own file because the failure aborts rather than accumulates:
// parseFilename's caller reaches errorExit(ExitNF), which terminates the
// compile on the spot, so nothing written after this line would ever be
// reached. The exit status is the whole assertion -- ExitNF is reported by
// errorExit, which prints no 'Error n:' header and so counts as no diagnostic.
//
// 'include' fails the same way through the same call.

import nosuchmodule

fn unreached() i64 {
  1i64
}
